The four steps
Natural selection needs four ingredients. (1) VARIATION: individuals differ (Module 4's meiosis guarantees it) — beak sizes, fur shades, enzyme variants. (2) COMPETITION: more offspring are born than can survive (a fish lays millions of eggs; the pond feeds hundreds). (3) DIFFERENTIAL SURVIVAL (selection): individuals whose variants suit the environment survive and breed more — nature 'selects' without intent. (4) INHERITANCE: survivors pass their alleles on, so helpful variants spread and the population's gene pool shifts. Repeat for thousands of generations and populations ADAPT — accumulating traits that fit their world. Darwin inferred this from barnacles, pigeons and Galápagos finches; modern genetics supplied the mechanism he lacked (DNA, mutation, meiosis).

Misconceptions to destroy
Three errors lose marks and mislead thinking. (1) 'Individuals evolve' — FALSE: individuals live or die; POPULATIONS evolve as allele frequencies shift. (2) 'Lamarck was right that use and disuse inherits' — FALSE: a blacksmith's muscles do not alter his sperm's DNA; acquired characteristics are NOT inherited (but note: the environment selects among inherited variants). (3) 'Evolution has a purpose or goal' — FALSE: selection is blind, with no foresight — it keeps whatever works NOW. Also reject 'survival of the strongest': it is survival of the FITTEST-TO-THIS-ENVIRONMENT — the fittest bacterium is the one that survives antibiotics, not the biggest. Use allele-frequency language in examinations: 'the resistance allele increased in frequency' beats 'bacteria got stronger'.$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["List the four requirements for natural selection","Explain antibiotic resistance as selection in action","Correct common misconceptions (Lamarck, purpose, individuals)"],"introduction":"In 1859 Darwin published an idea so powerful it united all of biology: species change because nature selects. No designer required — just variation, competition and time.","key_points":["Four steps in order","Allele-frequency language for exams","Selection sorts; mutation creates"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 18, Evolution and the Origin of Species"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod06$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod06:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_