The address system
HABITAT: where an organism lives (a fishpond, a mango canopy). POPULATION: all members of ONE species in a habitat (all tilapia in the pond). COMMUNITY: ALL populations sharing the habitat (tilapia + catfish + algae + water insects). ECOSYSTEM: community PLUS non-living surroundings (water, mud, sunlight, dissolved oxygen). BIOME: a continental-scale ecosystem type (tropical rainforest, savanna, desert). NICHE: an organism's ROLE — what it eats, what eats it, when it is active (no two species hold identical niches for long — competition excludes one). Factors splitting the world: BIOTIC (living: predation, competition, disease, food supply) and ABIOTIC (non-living: light, temperature, water, pH, salinity, oxygen). Examination habit: always classify factors before explaining effects.$wdthseed$, NULL, 25, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Define habitat, population, community, ecosystem and niche","Distinguish biotic from abiotic factors with examples","Explain how one abiotic factor limits a named population"],"introduction":"A tilapia's world is water temperature, dissolved oxygen, algae to eat and fishermen to avoid. Ecology maps these worlds — and what happens when they change.","key_points":["Five address levels in order","Biotic vs abiotic classification first","Temperature-oxygen solubility link"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 42, Ecosystems (levels of ecology)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod07$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod07:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
