Four impacts
(1) DEFORESTATION: logging, farming and fuelwood remove forests → biodiversity loss, soil erosion (no roots to hold soil), flooding, and CO2 release (fewer absorbers + burning). (2) POLLUTION: oil spills smother mangroves and fisheries (Niger Delta); plastic chokes drains and livestock; industrial effluent poisons rivers; vehicle exhaust harms lungs. (3) OVERHARVESTING: taking faster than replacement — overfishing collapses stocks (smaller catches yearly), bushmeat hunting empties forests ('empty forest syndrome'). (4) CLIMATE CHANGE: fossil-fuel CO2 traps heat → rising temperatures, erratic rainfall, sea-level rise threatening Lagos and the Delta, and shifting disease zones (malaria climbing to highlands). Each impact hits the poorest first — environmental damage is a justice issue.

Conservation that works
PRESERVATION locks nature away untouched; CONSERVATION manages use sustainably (harvest below replacement rate). Working tools: PROTECTED AREAS (Yankari, Cross River parks) guard biodiversity cores; REFORESTATION and agroforestry rebuild cover and income; SUSTAINABLE FISHING (size limits, closed seasons, no dynamite) lets stocks recover; WASTE MANAGEMENT (reduce, reuse, recycle; proper dumps, not drains); CLEAN ENERGY (solar leapfrogs grids); and EDUCATION — the multiplier of all the rest. Conservation succeeds when locals benefit: ecotourism jobs, beekeeping buffers, community forests. Your assignment investigates one local issue and proposes exactly such a plan.$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 5, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Explain four human impacts with mechanisms and effects","Distinguish conservation from preservation","Propose three realistic local conservation actions"],"introduction":"Nigeria loses hundreds of thousands of hectares of forest yearly; Lagos traffic chokes the air; the Sahel creeps south. Ecology without action is just watching — this lesson demands solutions.","key_points":["Four impacts with mechanisms","Conservation vs preservation","Solutions must benefit locals"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 44 (conservation biology)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod07$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod07:top03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
